The art/ folder holds the original game's pictures, converted from BMP to PNG:
balls.png, logo.png and gameover.png, by Michael Wulff Nielsen and Jeppe
Isaaksen, from BeSame 1.0 for BeOS (1999), which its author released as
freeware. BeSame.hvif is the icon from Michel Clasquin-Johnson's Haiku package
of the original. They are not covered by the MIT licence above; they are
redistributed as part of the freeware game, with credit to their authors. The
original's licence text, as it came with that package:

  Welcome to BeSame V1.0. This is a small puzzle game created by Michael Wulff
  Nielsen (Naish@get2net.dk) and betatested by Matthias Schonder. The
  objective of the game is to remove all the colored bricks from the board.
  This game is basically cloned from Same Gnome, which is part of the Gnome
  desktop environment on Linux. This game is freeware, but if you like it drop
  me a line at Naish@get2net.dk

  Disclaimer
  The author of this program can in no way be held responsible for any damage
  inadvertendly caused by the use of this software. Neither can the author be
  held responsible for any dataloss, that might occur. This program is
  delivered as is, and should not be harmfull to any beos installation.
